; kv64.cmhg - Kv64: a key/value store as a module: five SWIs (Kv64_Set Get Delete Count Enum, and Clear), four commands, the data in the RMA.  A worked example of a typical data module.
title-string: Kv64
help-string: Kv64 0.01
date-string: 18 Oct 2026
initialisation-code: kv_init
finalisation-code: kv_final
swi-chunk-base-number: 0x59C40
swi-handler-code: kv_swi
swi-decoding-table: Kv64 Set Get Delete Count Enum Clear
command-keyword-table: kv_command
  Kv_Set(min-args: 2, max-args: 2, help-text: "Kv_Set stores a value under a key.\r\n", invalid-syntax: "Syntax: *Kv_Set <key> <value>"),
  Kv_Get(min-args: 1, max-args: 1, help-text: "Kv_Get prints the value of a key.\r\n", invalid-syntax: "Syntax: *Kv_Get <key>"),
  Kv_List(min-args: 0, max-args: 0, help-text: "Kv_List prints all the keys and values.\r\n", invalid-syntax: "Syntax: *Kv_List"),
  Kv_Clear(min-args: 0, max-args: 0, help-text: "Kv_Clear removes all the keys.\r\n", invalid-syntax: "Syntax: *Kv_Clear")
